window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b396-5fbc3274b4de8380.json"]={sha256:"5fbc3274b4de838019595cbf78a672d27b59725c6dd14e2daa1fd3060fe0e5f0",value:{"id":"b396","title":"無架空線輕軌供電","titleEn":"Catenary-free light-rail power systems","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦區分分段地面供電與車載儲能的無架空線系統。從輪周功率與電源需求建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把輔助供電的跨區續航與電源模式交接時序連成可驗證的介面，最後以線路服務與設備修復整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies distinguishing segmented ground supply from onboard energy storage. Start with wheel power and supply demand to define physical or information boundaries, connect auxiliary backup across supply gaps with power-mode handoff timing as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through line service and equipment recovery. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-power","subcategoryTitle":"牽引供電與受流","subcategoryTitleEn":"Traction power and current collection","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-power","learningTags":["rail","rail-power","power"],"architectureFamily":"rail-integration","architectureNodes":[["地面饋電","Ground supply"],["車載儲能","Onboard storage"],["牽引負載","Traction load"],["能量量測","Energy measurement"],["狀態證據","State evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-integration","labels":["地面饋電","車載儲能","牽引負載","能量量測","狀態證據"],"labelsEn":["Ground supply","Onboard storage","Traction load","Energy measurement","State evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究輪周功率與電源需求。原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。公式 y=(m*a+R)*v/1000，代入得 y=1800 kW。邊界：集中質量與定阻力模型，未含輪軸轉動慣量、坡度或黏著上限。敏感度只改 m=180000 至 198000 kg，輸出變為 1962 kW；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究回生能量與接收邊界：原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。公式 y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6，代入得 y=8.47 kWh。邊界：忽略旋轉動能、坡度位能及輔機，效率固定且假設有足夠受納容量。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。先以車輛加速和阻力建立輪周機械功率，再另列供電轉換與輔機損失。比較同速度下不同載重需求，不把車載電流直接等同於有效牽引力。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate wheel power and supply demand. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s. Formula y=(m*a+R)*v/1000 gives y=1800 kW. Boundary: Lumped mass and fixed resistance; rotating inertia, gradient and adhesion limits are omitted. For sensitivity, change only m=180000 to 198000 kg; the output becomes 1962 kW. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate regeneration and receiving boundaries: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1. Formula y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6 gives y=8.47 kWh. Boundary: Rotating energy, elevation and auxiliaries are omitted; efficiency is constant and receiving capacity is assumed adequate. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Establish wheel mechanical power from acceleration and resistance before accounting for conversion and auxiliary losses. Compare loads at the same speed without treating supply current as effective tractive effort. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b396-v16-s1","title":"輪周功率與電源需求與回生能量與接收邊界","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand & Regeneration and receiving boundaries","description":"本階段聚焦「輪周功率與電源需求」與「回生能量與接收邊界」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wheel power and supply demand\" and \"Regeneration and receiving boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b396-v16-01","title":"輪周功率與電源需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「輪周功率與電源需求」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wheel power and supply demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"先以車輛加速和阻力建立輪周機械功率，再另列供電轉換與輔機損失。比較同速度下不同載重需求，不把車載電流直接等同於有效牽引力。牽引力先克服阻力，剩餘部分才增加列車動量。輪周機械功率等於牽引力乘速度，因此低速大力不必然等於高功率；電源側功率另受效率、輔助負載及回生可受納性影響。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：集中質量與定阻力模型，未含輪軸轉動慣量、坡度或黏著上限。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輪周功率與電源需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Establish wheel mechanical power from acceleration and resistance before accounting for conversion and auxiliary losses. Compare loads at the same speed without treating supply current as effective tractive effort. Traction force first overcomes resistance; the remainder changes train momentum. Mechanical power at the wheel equals force times speed, so a large low-speed force need not imply high power. Electrical input also depends on efficiency, auxiliaries and regenerative receptivity. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Lumped mass and fixed resistance; rotating inertia, gradient and adhesion limits are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wheel power and supply demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輪周功率與電源需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wheel power and supply demand”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-01-k1","title":"輪周功率與電源需求","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand","text":"先以車輛加速和阻力建立輪周機械功率，再另列供電轉換與輔機損失。比較同速度下不同載重需求，不把車載電流直接等同於有效牽引力。","textEn":"Establish wheel mechanical power from acceleration and resistance before accounting for conversion and auxiliary losses. Compare loads at the same speed without treating supply current as effective tractive effort.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輪周功率與電源需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wheel power and supply demand\" is correct?","options":["牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快","先以車輛加速和阻力建立輪周機械功率，再另列供電轉換與輔機損失。","有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱"],"optionsEn":["Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration.","Establish wheel mechanical power from acceleration and resistance before accounting for conversion and auxiliary losses.","A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先以車輛加速和阻力建立輪周機械功率，再另列供電轉換與輔機損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Establish wheel mechanical power from acceleration and resistance before accounting for conversion and auxiliary losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b396-v16-02","title":"輪周功率與電源需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輪周功率與電源需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wheel power and supply demand” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。公式 y=(m*a+R)*v/1000，代入得 y=1800 kW。邊界：集中質量與定阻力模型，未含輪軸轉動慣量、坡度或黏著上限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s. Formula y=(m*a+R)*v/1000 gives y=1800 kW. Boundary: Lumped mass and fixed resistance; rotating inertia, gradient and adhesion limits are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將速度與牽引力同步取樣，對照加速度反推的慣性力，並另列輔助設備耗電。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize speed and traction-force samples, compare inertial force inferred from acceleration, and account separately for auxiliary consumption.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。公式 y=(m*a+R)*v/1000，代入得 y=1800 kW。邊界：集中質量與定阻力模型，未含輪軸轉動慣量、坡度或黏著上限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s. Formula y=(m*a+R)*v/1000 gives y=1800 kW. Boundary: Lumped mass and fixed resistance; rotating inertia, gradient and adhesion limits are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輪周功率與電源需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wheel power and supply demand\", which statement holds?","options":["只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：列車質量 m=180000 kg；加速度 a=0.6 m/s2；等效阻力 R=12000 N；速度 v=15 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: train mass m=180000 kg; acceleration a=0.6 m/s2; equivalent resistance R=12000 N; speed v=15 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b396-v16-03","title":"輪周功率與電源需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輪周功率與電源需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wheel power and supply demand” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將速度與牽引力同步取樣，對照加速度反推的慣性力，並另列輔助設備耗電。以「輪周功率與電源需求」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize speed and traction-force samples, compare inertial force inferred from acceleration, and account separately for auxiliary consumption. For wheel power and supply demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把列車質量 m 從 180000 改成 198000 kg（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1800 變為 1962 kW。先說明「輪周功率與電源需求」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only train mass m from 180000 to 198000 kg (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1800 to 1962 kW. Explain the causal direction for wheel power and supply demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把電網輸入功率直接當成輪周功率會高估加速能力，低速輪滑亦可使電流很高而車速不升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating grid input as wheel power overstates acceleration capability; low-speed slip can produce high current without increasing train speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將速度與牽引力同步取樣，對照加速度反推的慣性力，並另列輔助設備耗電。以「輪周功率與電源需求」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Synchronize speed and traction-force samples, compare inertial force inferred from acceleration, and account separately for auxiliary consumption. For wheel power and supply demand, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把列車質量 m 從 180000 改成 198000 kg（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1800 變為 1962 kW。先說明「輪周功率與電源需求」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only train mass m from 180000 to 198000 kg (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1800 to 1962 kW. Explain the causal direction for wheel power and supply demand, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輪周功率與電源需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wheel power and supply demand\"?","options":["將速度與牽引力同步取樣，對照加速度反推的慣性力，並另列輔助設備耗電。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize speed and traction-force samples, compare inertial force inferred from acceleration, and account separately for auxiliary consumption.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將速度與牽引力同步取樣，對照加速度反推的慣性力，並另列輔助設備耗電。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize speed and traction-force samples, compare inertial force inferred from acceleration, and account separately for auxiliary consumption. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b396-v16-04","title":"輪周功率與電源需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wheel power and supply demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輪周功率與電源需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wheel power and supply demand” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把電網輸入功率直接當成輪周功率會高估加速能力，低速輪滑亦可使電流很高而車速不升。回到「輪周功率與電源需求」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating grid input as wheel power overstates acceleration capability; low-speed slip can produce high current without increasing train speed. Trace the input chain for wheel power and supply demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：集中質量與定阻力模型，未含輪軸轉動慣量、坡度或黏著上限。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Lumped mass and fixed resistance; rotating inertia, gradient and adhesion limits are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把電網輸入功率直接當成輪周功率會高估加速能力，低速輪滑亦可使電流很高而車速不升。回到「輪周功率與電源需求」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Treating grid input as wheel power overstates acceleration capability; low-speed slip can produce high current without increasing train speed. Trace the input chain for wheel power and supply demand. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輪周功率與電源需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wheel power and supply demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把電網輸入功率直接當成輪周功率會高估加速能力，低速輪滑亦可使電流很高而車速不升。","有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating grid input as wheel power overstates acceleration capability; low-speed slip can produce high current without increasing train speed.","A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把電網輸入功率直接當成輪周功率會高估加速能力，低速輪滑亦可使電流很高而車速不升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating grid input as wheel power overstates acceleration capability; low-speed slip can produce high current without increasing train speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b396-v16-05","title":"回生能量與接收邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Regeneration and receiving boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「回生能量與接收邊界」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Regeneration and receiving boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把列車動能上限、轉換效率和接收能力分開，辨認能量究竟回到電網還是車載儲能。接收端不可用時不能假設全部回收，能量帳仍要列出耗散去向。回生能量的上限先受列車動能限制，再受轉換損失與受電端容量限制。速度平方決定動能量級，回生率不能單獨說明整趟能耗；若鄰車或儲能無法接收，原可回收的能量仍可能轉為電阻熱。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：忽略旋轉動能、坡度位能及輔機，效率固定且假設有足夠受納容量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回生能量與接收邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate kinetic-energy limit, conversion efficiency and receptivity, identifying grid and onboard storage as different receivers. When reception is unavailable, retain the dissipation path instead of assuming complete recovery. Recoverable energy is bounded first by kinetic energy and then by conversion losses and receiver capacity. The square of speed sets the energy scale, while recovery efficiency alone cannot describe journey consumption. Energy may still become resistor heat when nearby trains or storage cannot accept it. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Rotating energy, elevation and auxiliaries are omitted; efficiency is constant and receiving capacity is assumed adequate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Regeneration and receiving boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回生能量與接收邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Regeneration and receiving boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-05-k1","title":"回生能量與接收邊界","titleEn":"Regeneration and receiving boundaries","text":"把列車動能上限、轉換效率和接收能力分開，辨認能量究竟回到電網還是車載儲能。接收端不可用時不能假設全部回收，能量帳仍要列出耗散去向。","textEn":"Separate kinetic-energy limit, conversion efficiency and receptivity, identifying grid and onboard storage as different receivers. When reception is unavailable, retain the dissipation path instead of assuming complete recovery.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回生能量與接收邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Regeneration and receiving boundaries\" is correct?","options":["有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱","直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍","把列車動能上限、轉換效率和接收能力分開，辨認能量究竟回到電網還是車載儲能。"],"optionsEn":["A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat.","Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.","Separate kinetic-energy limit, conversion efficiency and receptivity, identifying grid and onboard storage as different receivers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把列車動能上限、轉換效率和接收能力分開，辨認能量究竟回到電網還是車載儲能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate kinetic-energy limit, conversion efficiency and receptivity, identifying grid and onboard storage as different receivers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b396-v16-06","title":"回生能量與接收邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Regeneration and receiving boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回生能量與接收邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Regeneration and receiving boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。公式 y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6，代入得 y=8.47 kWh。邊界：忽略旋轉動能、坡度位能及輔機，效率固定且假設有足夠受納容量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1. Formula y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6 gives y=8.47 kWh. Boundary: Rotating energy, elevation and auxiliaries are omitted; efficiency is constant and receiving capacity is assumed adequate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較電機側與直流母線能量積分，分開記錄制動電阻消耗與儲能充電。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare integrated machine-side and DC-bus energy, keeping braking-resistor dissipation distinct from energy stored.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。公式 y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6，代入得 y=8.47 kWh。邊界：忽略旋轉動能、坡度位能及輔機，效率固定且假設有足夠受納容量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1. Formula y=0.5*m*v*v*eta/3.6e6 gives y=8.47 kWh. Boundary: Rotating energy, elevation and auxiliaries are omitted; efficiency is constant and receiving capacity is assumed adequate.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回生能量與接收邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Regeneration and receiving boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。","外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1.","A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：等效質量 m=180000 kg；速度 v=22 m/s；回收效率 eta=0.7 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: equivalent mass m=180000 kg; speed v=22 m/s; recovery efficiency eta=0.7 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b396-v16-07","title":"回生能量與接收邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Regeneration and receiving boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回生能量與接收邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Regeneration and receiving boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較電機側與直流母線能量積分，分開記錄制動電阻消耗與儲能充電。以「回生能量與接收邊界」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare integrated machine-side and DC-bus energy, keeping braking-resistor dissipation distinct from energy stored. For regeneration and receiving boundaries, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把速度 v 從 22 改成 24.2 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8.47 變為 10.2487 kWh。先說明「回生能量與接收邊界」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only speed v from 22 to 24.2 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8.47 to 10.2487 kWh. Explain the causal direction for regeneration and receiving boundaries, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：電壓過高限制回生時，制動力仍可能由混合制動維持，不能由低回收量直接判定制動失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High bus voltage can restrict regeneration while blended braking preserves stopping effort; low recovered energy alone does not prove brake failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較電機側與直流母線能量積分，分開記錄制動電阻消耗與儲能充電。以「回生能量與接收邊界」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Compare integrated machine-side and DC-bus energy, keeping braking-resistor dissipation distinct from energy stored. For regeneration and receiving boundaries, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把速度 v 從 22 改成 24.2 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 8.47 變為 10.2487 kWh。先說明「回生能量與接收邊界」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only speed v from 22 to 24.2 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 8.47 to 10.2487 kWh. Explain the causal direction for regeneration and receiving boundaries, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回生能量與接收邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Regeneration and receiving boundaries\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較電機側與直流母線能量積分，分開記錄制動電阻消耗與儲能充電。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare integrated machine-side and DC-bus energy, keeping braking-resistor dissipation distinct from energy stored.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較電機側與直流母線能量積分，分開記錄制動電阻消耗與儲能充電。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare integrated machine-side and DC-bus energy, keeping braking-resistor dissipation distinct from energy stored. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b396-v16-08","title":"回生能量與接收邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Regeneration and receiving boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回生能量與接收邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Regeneration and receiving boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"電壓過高限制回生時，制動力仍可能由混合制動維持，不能由低回收量直接判定制動失效。回到「回生能量與接收邊界」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High bus voltage can restrict regeneration while blended braking preserves stopping effort; low recovered energy alone does not prove brake failure. Trace the input chain for regeneration and receiving boundaries. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：忽略旋轉動能、坡度位能及輔機，效率固定且假設有足夠受納容量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Rotating energy, elevation and auxiliaries are omitted; efficiency is constant and receiving capacity is assumed adequate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"電壓過高限制回生時，制動力仍可能由混合制動維持，不能由低回收量直接判定制動失效。回到「回生能量與接收邊界」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"High bus voltage can restrict regeneration while blended braking preserves stopping effort; low recovered energy alone does not prove brake failure. Trace the input chain for regeneration and receiving boundaries. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回生能量與接收邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Regeneration and receiving boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍","電壓過高限制回生時，制動力仍可能由混合制動維持，不能由低回收量直接判定制動失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.","High bus voltage can restrict regeneration while blended braking preserves stopping effort; low recovered energy alone does not prove brake failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電壓過高限制回生時，制動力仍可能由混合制動維持，不能由低回收量直接判定制動失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High bus voltage can restrict regeneration while blended braking preserves stopping effort; low recovered energy alone does not prove brake failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b396-v16-s2","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失與輔助供電的跨區續航","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts & Auxiliary backup across supply gaps","description":"本階段聚焦「導體接觸的電阻損失」與「輔助供電的跨區續航」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts\" and \"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b396-v16-09","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「導體接觸的電阻損失」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在理想直流回路中以電流平方比較電阻損失，區分有用牽引功率與局部發熱。接觸劣化會改變電阻與熱點位置，量測需同時保留電流和壓降。直流饋電與接觸路徑的電阻損耗與電流平方成正比，所以尖峰電流對發熱特別敏感。等效電阻可包含導線與接點，卻不能把各部位的散熱條件視為相同；平均總損耗正常仍可能有局部接點過熱，分段供電的安全狀態也不是由此功率公式決定。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：理想穩態直流電阻損耗，未提供地面供電分段邏輯或現場帶電作業方法。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導體接觸的電阻損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use current squared to compare resistive loss in an ideal DC path, separating useful traction power from local heating. Retain current and voltage-drop measurements as contact deterioration changes resistance and hotspot location. Resistive loss in a DC feeder and contact path scales with current squared, making peak current particularly influential. Equivalent resistance may include conductors and contacts, but their cooling conditions differ. A normal total loss can coexist with a hot contact, and the safe state of segmented supply is not determined by this power equation. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Ideal steady DC resistance loss, without ground-supply segmentation logic or live electrical work procedures. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：假想直流電流 I=200 A；等效回路電阻 R=0.03 ohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: assumed direct current I=200 A; equivalent circuit resistance R=0.03 ohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導體接觸的電阻損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-09-k1","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts","text":"在理想直流回路中以電流平方比較電阻損失，區分有用牽引功率與局部發熱。接觸劣化會改變電阻與熱點位置，量測需同時保留電流和壓降。","textEn":"Use current squared to compare resistive loss in an ideal DC path, separating useful traction power from local heating. Retain current and voltage-drop measurements as contact deterioration changes resistance and hotspot location.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導體接觸的電阻損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts\" is correct?","options":["在理想直流回路中以電流平方比較電阻損失，區分有用牽引功率與局部發熱。","直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍","只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同"],"optionsEn":["Use current squared to compare resistive loss in an ideal DC path, separating useful traction power from local heating.","Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.","Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在理想直流回路中以電流平方比較電阻損失，區分有用牽引功率與局部發熱。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use current squared to compare resistive loss in an ideal DC path, separating useful traction power from local heating. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b396-v16-10","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導體接觸的電阻損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：假想直流電流 I=200 A；等效回路電阻 R=0.03 ohm。公式 y=I*I*R/1000，代入得 y=1.2 kW。邊界：理想穩態直流電阻損耗，未提供地面供電分段邏輯或現場帶電作業方法。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: assumed direct current I=200 A; equivalent circuit resistance R=0.03 ohm. Formula y=I*I*R/1000 gives y=1.2 kW. Boundary: Ideal steady DC resistance loss, without ground-supply segmentation logic or live electrical work procedures. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在隔離低壓台同時量測電流與電壓降，核對功率帳後以溫度分布尋找局部接觸電阻異常。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure current and voltage drop together on an isolated low-voltage rig, check power balance, and use temperature distribution to locate abnormal contact resistance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：假想直流電流 I=200 A；等效回路電阻 R=0.03 ohm。公式 y=I*I*R/1000，代入得 y=1.2 kW。邊界：理想穩態直流電阻損耗，未提供地面供電分段邏輯或現場帶電作業方法。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: assumed direct current I=200 A; equivalent circuit resistance R=0.03 ohm. Formula y=I*I*R/1000 gives y=1.2 kW. Boundary: Ideal steady DC resistance loss, without ground-supply segmentation logic or live electrical work procedures.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導體接觸的電阻損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts\", which statement holds?","options":["狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","原創假想教學輸入：假想直流電流 I=200 A；等效回路電阻 R=0.03 ohm。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: assumed direct current I=200 A; equivalent circuit resistance R=0.03 ohm.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：假想直流電流 I=200 A；等效回路電阻 R=0.03 ohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: assumed direct current I=200 A; equivalent circuit resistance R=0.03 ohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b396-v16-11","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導體接觸的電阻損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在隔離低壓台同時量測電流與電壓降，核對功率帳後以溫度分布尋找局部接觸電阻異常。以「導體接觸的電阻損失」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure current and voltage drop together on an isolated low-voltage rig, check power balance, and use temperature distribution to locate abnormal contact resistance. For resistive losses in conductors and contacts, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把假想直流電流 I 從 200 改成 220 A（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.2 變為 1.452 kW。先說明「導體接觸的電阻損失」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only assumed direct current I from 200 to 220 A (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.2 to 1.452 kW. Explain the causal direction for resistive losses in conductors and contacts, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：鬆動接點會把損耗集中在小區域，平均回路電阻的低解析度量測可能漏掉隨振動發生的間歇接觸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A loose contact concentrates loss in a small region; low-resolution mean resistance measurement can miss intermittent contact changes under vibration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在隔離低壓台同時量測電流與電壓降，核對功率帳後以溫度分布尋找局部接觸電阻異常。以「導體接觸的電阻損失」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure current and voltage drop together on an isolated low-voltage rig, check power balance, and use temperature distribution to locate abnormal contact resistance. For resistive losses in conductors and contacts, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把假想直流電流 I 從 200 改成 220 A（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 1.2 變為 1.452 kW。先說明「導體接觸的電阻損失」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only assumed direct current I from 200 to 220 A (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 1.2 to 1.452 kW. Explain the causal direction for resistive losses in conductors and contacts, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導體接觸的電阻損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","在隔離低壓台同時量測電流與電壓降，核對功率帳後以溫度分布尋找局部接觸電阻異常。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","Measure current and voltage drop together on an isolated low-voltage rig, check power balance, and use temperature distribution to locate abnormal contact resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在隔離低壓台同時量測電流與電壓降，核對功率帳後以溫度分布尋找局部接觸電阻異常。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure current and voltage drop together on an isolated low-voltage rig, check power balance, and use temperature distribution to locate abnormal contact resistance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b396-v16-12","title":"導體接觸的電阻損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導體接觸的電阻損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resistive losses in conductors and contacts” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鬆動接點會把損耗集中在小區域，平均回路電阻的低解析度量測可能漏掉隨振動發生的間歇接觸。回到「導體接觸的電阻損失」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A loose contact concentrates loss in a small region; low-resolution mean resistance measurement can miss intermittent contact changes under vibration. Trace the input chain for resistive losses in conductors and contacts. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：理想穩態直流電阻損耗，未提供地面供電分段邏輯或現場帶電作業方法。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Ideal steady DC resistance loss, without ground-supply segmentation logic or live electrical work procedures.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鬆動接點會把損耗集中在小區域，平均回路電阻的低解析度量測可能漏掉隨振動發生的間歇接觸。回到「導體接觸的電阻損失」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"A loose contact concentrates loss in a small region; low-resolution mean resistance measurement can miss intermittent contact changes under vibration. Trace the input chain for resistive losses in conductors and contacts. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導體接觸的電阻損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resistive losses in conductors and contacts\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鬆動接點會把損耗集中在小區域，平均回路電阻的低解析度量測可能漏掉隨振動發生的間歇接觸。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同"],"optionsEn":["A loose contact concentrates loss in a small region; low-resolution mean resistance measurement can miss intermittent contact changes under vibration.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鬆動接點會把損耗集中在小區域，平均回路電阻的低解析度量測可能漏掉隨振動發生的間歇接觸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A loose contact concentrates loss in a small region; low-resolution mean resistance measurement can miss intermittent contact changes under vibration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b396-v16-13","title":"輔助供電的跨區續航：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「輔助供電的跨區續航」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"此單元只估控制和監視負載的定電壓備援時間，不代表車輛主牽引續航。先列可用能量比例，再討論負載尖峰與老化如何讓平均能量估算失準。電池續航以可用能量除以負載估算，容量不能只看安培小時而忽略電壓。溫度、老化、放電速率與截止電壓都影響可用比例；緊急供電還需檢查負載啟動尖峰，平均能量充足不代表瞬間電壓不會崩落。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定電壓定負載近似，未含電池非線性放電與溫度效應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「輔助供電的跨區續航」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Estimate constant-voltage backup for controls and monitoring only, not main traction range. State usable-energy fraction before discussing surges and ageing that can defeat an average-energy estimate. Battery duration divides usable energy by load, so ampere-hours alone are insufficient without voltage. Temperature, ageing, discharge rate and cutoff affect usable fraction. Emergency supply must also handle starting surges; sufficient average energy does not guarantee stable instantaneous voltage. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-voltage constant-load approximation; nonlinear discharge and temperature effects are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：額定容量 capacity=80 Ah；標稱電壓 voltage=24 V；可用比例 fraction=0.7 1；固定負載 load=350 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: rated capacity capacity=80 Ah; nominal voltage voltage=24 V; usable fraction fraction=0.7 1; constant load load=350 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「輔助供電的跨區續航」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-13-k1","title":"輔助供電的跨區續航","titleEn":"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps","text":"此單元只估控制和監視負載的定電壓備援時間，不代表車輛主牽引續航。先列可用能量比例，再討論負載尖峰與老化如何讓平均能量估算失準。","textEn":"Estimate constant-voltage backup for controls and monitoring only, not main traction range. State usable-energy fraction before discussing surges and ageing that can defeat an average-energy estimate.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輔助供電的跨區續航」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps\" is correct?","options":["只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同","此單元只估控制和監視負載的定電壓備援時間，不代表車輛主牽引續航。","外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱"],"optionsEn":["Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries.","Estimate constant-voltage backup for controls and monitoring only, not main traction range.","A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"此單元只估控制和監視負載的定電壓備援時間，不代表車輛主牽引續航。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Estimate constant-voltage backup for controls and monitoring only, not main traction range. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b396-v16-14","title":"輔助供電的跨區續航：定量估算","titleEn":"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「輔助供電的跨區續航」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：額定容量 capacity=80 Ah；標稱電壓 voltage=24 V；可用比例 fraction=0.7 1；固定負載 load=350 W。公式 y=capacity*voltage*fraction/load，代入得 y=3.84 h。邊界：定電壓定負載近似，未含電池非線性放電與溫度效應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: rated capacity capacity=80 Ah; nominal voltage voltage=24 V; usable fraction fraction=0.7 1; constant load load=350 W. Formula y=capacity*voltage*fraction/load gives y=3.84 h. Boundary: Constant-voltage constant-load approximation; nonlinear discharge and temperature effects are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測完整負載曲線與最低端電壓，分別核對連續能量及啟動瞬間壓降。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the load profile and minimum terminal voltage, checking continuous energy and startup sag separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：額定容量 capacity=80 Ah；標稱電壓 voltage=24 V；可用比例 fraction=0.7 1；固定負載 load=350 W。公式 y=capacity*voltage*fraction/load，代入得 y=3.84 h。邊界：定電壓定負載近似，未含電池非線性放電與溫度效應。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: rated capacity capacity=80 Ah; nominal voltage voltage=24 V; usable fraction fraction=0.7 1; constant load load=350 W. Formula y=capacity*voltage*fraction/load gives y=3.84 h. Boundary: Constant-voltage constant-load approximation; nonlinear discharge and temperature effects are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輔助供電的跨區續航」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps\", which statement holds?","options":["每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：額定容量 capacity=80 Ah。"],"optionsEn":["Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: rated capacity capacity=80 Ah; nominal voltage voltage=24 V; usable fraction fraction=0.7 1; constant load load=350 W."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：額定容量 capacity=80 Ah；標稱電壓 voltage=24 V；可用比例 fraction=0.7 1；固定負載 load=350 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: rated capacity capacity=80 Ah; nominal voltage voltage=24 V; usable fraction fraction=0.7 1; constant load load=350 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b396-v16-15","title":"輔助供電的跨區續航：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「輔助供電的跨區續航」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測完整負載曲線與最低端電壓，分別核對連續能量及啟動瞬間壓降。以「輔助供電的跨區續航」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the load profile and minimum terminal voltage, checking continuous energy and startup sag separately. For auxiliary backup across supply gaps, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把固定負載 load 從 350 改成 385 W（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 3.84 變為 3.49091 h。先說明「輔助供電的跨區續航」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only constant load load from 350 to 385 W (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 3.84 to 3.49091 h. Explain the causal direction for auxiliary backup across supply gaps, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：老化電池可能保有部分容量但內阻升高，啟動負載時掉壓使設備提早中止。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An aged battery may retain some capacity while internal resistance rises, causing early shutdown during a starting load. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測完整負載曲線與最低端電壓，分別核對連續能量及啟動瞬間壓降。以「輔助供電的跨區續航」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure the load profile and minimum terminal voltage, checking continuous energy and startup sag separately. For auxiliary backup across supply gaps, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把固定負載 load 從 350 改成 385 W（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 3.84 變為 3.49091 h。先說明「輔助供電的跨區續航」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only constant load load from 350 to 385 W (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 3.84 to 3.49091 h. Explain the causal direction for auxiliary backup across supply gaps, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輔助供電的跨區續航」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps\"?","options":["量測完整負載曲線與最低端電壓，分別核對連續能量及啟動瞬間壓降。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快"],"optionsEn":["Measure the load profile and minimum terminal voltage, checking continuous energy and startup sag separately.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測完整負載曲線與最低端電壓，分別核對連續能量及啟動瞬間壓降。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the load profile and minimum terminal voltage, checking continuous energy and startup sag separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b396-v16-16","title":"輔助供電的跨區續航：失效診斷","titleEn":"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「輔助供電的跨區續航」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Auxiliary backup across supply gaps” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"老化電池可能保有部分容量但內阻升高，啟動負載時掉壓使設備提早中止。回到「輔助供電的跨區續航」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An aged battery may retain some capacity while internal resistance rises, causing early shutdown during a starting load. Trace the input chain for auxiliary backup across supply gaps. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定電壓定負載近似，未含電池非線性放電與溫度效應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant-voltage constant-load approximation; nonlinear discharge and temperature effects are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"老化電池可能保有部分容量但內阻升高，啟動負載時掉壓使設備提早中止。回到「輔助供電的跨區續航」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"An aged battery may retain some capacity while internal resistance rises, causing early shutdown during a starting load. Trace the input chain for auxiliary backup across supply gaps. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輔助供電的跨區續航」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Auxiliary backup across supply gaps\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","老化電池可能保有部分容量但內阻升高，啟動負載時掉壓使設備提早中止。","外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An aged battery may retain some capacity while internal resistance rises, causing early shutdown during a starting load.","A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"老化電池可能保有部分容量但內阻升高，啟動負載時掉壓使設備提早中止。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An aged battery may retain some capacity while internal resistance rises, causing early shutdown during a starting load. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b396-v16-s3","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界與供電區段與車載模式","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters & Supply-section and onboard states","description":"本階段聚焦「車載轉換器散熱邊界」與「供電區段與車載模式」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters\" and \"Supply-section and onboard states\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b396-v16-17","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「車載轉換器散熱邊界」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以平均損失功率估算轉換器穩態熱點，將環境溫度和散熱路徑分開改變。相同負載下的溫升差異可提示熱阻變化，但此模型不預測每次通過區段的瞬態峰值。穩態溫升由發熱乘等效熱阻決定，散熱路徑和熱源功率同樣重要。風道阻塞、接觸面鬆動與環境升溫都可能造成相同的最高溫度；若只換大風機而不追蹤熱路，可能改善外殼卻讓內部熱點繼續惡化。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：單節點線性穩態熱阻模型，未解析空間熱點與瞬態熱容。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「車載轉換器散熱邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Estimate steady converter temperature from mean loss and vary ambient and heat paths separately. Temperature differences can reveal thermal-resistance changes, but the model does not predict each segment-transition transient. Steady temperature rise equals heat generation times thermal resistance, making heat paths as important as source power. Blocked airflow, loose interfaces and warmer ambient conditions can produce similar maxima. A larger fan may cool the enclosure while an internal hotspot continues to worsen. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Single-node linear steady thermal-resistance model without spatial hotspots or transient heat capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：持續發熱 P=900 W；等效熱阻 Rth=0.035 K/W；環境溫度 ambient=30 degC。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: continuous heat P=900 W; equivalent thermal resistance Rth=0.035 K/W; ambient temperature ambient=30 degC.","failure":"常見誤解：「外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-17-k1","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters","text":"以平均損失功率估算轉換器穩態熱點，將環境溫度和散熱路徑分開改變。相同負載下的溫升差異可提示熱阻變化，但此模型不預測每次通過區段的瞬態峰值。","textEn":"Estimate steady converter temperature from mean loss and vary ambient and heat paths separately. Temperature differences can reveal thermal-resistance changes, but the model does not predict each segment-transition transient.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「車載轉換器散熱邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters\" is correct?","options":["外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","以平均損失功率估算轉換器穩態熱點，將環境溫度和散熱路徑分開改變。"],"optionsEn":["A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Estimate steady converter temperature from mean loss and vary ambient and heat paths separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以平均損失功率估算轉換器穩態熱點，將環境溫度和散熱路徑分開改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Estimate steady converter temperature from mean loss and vary ambient and heat paths separately. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b396-v16-18","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：持續發熱 P=900 W；等效熱阻 Rth=0.035 K/W；環境溫度 ambient=30 degC。公式 y=ambient+P*Rth，代入得 y=61.5 degC。邊界：單節點線性穩態熱阻模型，未解析空間熱點與瞬態熱容。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: continuous heat P=900 W; equivalent thermal resistance Rth=0.035 K/W; ambient temperature ambient=30 degC. Formula y=ambient+P*Rth gives y=61.5 degC. Boundary: Single-node linear steady thermal-resistance model without spatial hotspots or transient heat capacity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時記錄功率、環境與多點溫度，改變一項邊界條件以辨認熱源與熱阻變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record power, ambient and several temperatures together, changing one boundary to distinguish source and resistance changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：持續發熱 P=900 W；等效熱阻 Rth=0.035 K/W；環境溫度 ambient=30 degC。公式 y=ambient+P*Rth，代入得 y=61.5 degC。邊界：單節點線性穩態熱阻模型，未解析空間熱點與瞬態熱容。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: continuous heat P=900 W; equivalent thermal resistance Rth=0.035 K/W; ambient temperature ambient=30 degC. Formula y=ambient+P*Rth gives y=61.5 degC. Boundary: Single-node linear steady thermal-resistance model without spatial hotspots or transient heat capacity.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：持續發熱 P=900 W；等效熱阻 Rth=0.035 K/W；環境溫度 ambient=30 degC。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: continuous heat P=900 W; equivalent thermal resistance Rth=0.035 K/W; ambient temperature ambient=30 degC.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：持續發熱 P=900 W；等效熱阻 Rth=0.035 K/W；環境溫度 ambient=30 degC。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: continuous heat P=900 W; equivalent thermal resistance Rth=0.035 K/W; ambient temperature ambient=30 degC. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b396-v16-19","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「車載轉換器散熱邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時記錄功率、環境與多點溫度，改變一項邊界條件以辨認熱源與熱阻變化。以「車載轉換器散熱邊界」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record power, ambient and several temperatures together, changing one boundary to distinguish source and resistance changes. For cooling boundaries of onboard converters, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把等效熱阻 Rth 從 0.035 改成 0.0385 K/W（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 61.5 變為 64.65 degC。先說明「車載轉換器散熱邊界」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only equivalent thermal resistance Rth from 0.035 to 0.0385 K/W (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 61.5 to 64.65 degC. Explain the causal direction for cooling boundaries of onboard converters, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：環境感測器放在熱排氣中會把自身熱源誤當室溫升高，遮蔽熱點又會低估最大元件溫度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An ambient sensor in hot exhaust mistakes self-heating for room temperature rise, while hidden hotspots understate component maxima. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時記錄功率、環境與多點溫度，改變一項邊界條件以辨認熱源與熱阻變化。以「車載轉換器散熱邊界」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record power, ambient and several temperatures together, changing one boundary to distinguish source and resistance changes. For cooling boundaries of onboard converters, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把等效熱阻 Rth 從 0.035 改成 0.0385 K/W（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 61.5 變為 64.65 degC。先說明「車載轉換器散熱邊界」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only equivalent thermal resistance Rth from 0.035 to 0.0385 K/W (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 61.5 to 64.65 degC. Explain the causal direction for cooling boundaries of onboard converters, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「車載轉換器散熱邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同時記錄功率、環境與多點溫度，改變一項邊界條件以辨認熱源與熱阻變化。","有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record power, ambient and several temperatures together, changing one boundary to distinguish source and resistance changes.","A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同時記錄功率、環境與多點溫度，改變一項邊界條件以辨認熱源與熱阻變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record power, ambient and several temperatures together, changing one boundary to distinguish source and resistance changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b396-v16-20","title":"車載轉換器散熱邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cooling boundaries of onboard converters” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"環境感測器放在熱排氣中會把自身熱源誤當室溫升高，遮蔽熱點又會低估最大元件溫度。回到「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An ambient sensor in hot exhaust mistakes self-heating for room temperature rise, while hidden hotspots understate component maxima. Trace the input chain for cooling boundaries of onboard converters. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：單節點線性穩態熱阻模型，未解析空間熱點與瞬態熱容。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Single-node linear steady thermal-resistance model without spatial hotspots or transient heat capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"環境感測器放在熱排氣中會把自身熱源誤當室溫升高，遮蔽熱點又會低估最大元件溫度。回到「車載轉換器散熱邊界」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"An ambient sensor in hot exhaust mistakes self-heating for room temperature rise, while hidden hotspots understate component maxima. Trace the input chain for cooling boundaries of onboard converters. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「車載轉換器散熱邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cooling boundaries of onboard converters\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","環境感測器放在熱排氣中會把自身熱源誤當室溫升高，遮蔽熱點又會低估最大元件溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","An ambient sensor in hot exhaust mistakes self-heating for room temperature rise, while hidden hotspots understate component maxima."],"answer":2,"explanation":"環境感測器放在熱排氣中會把自身熱源誤當室溫升高，遮蔽熱點又會低估最大元件溫度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An ambient sensor in hot exhaust mistakes self-heating for room temperature rise, while hidden hotspots understate component maxima. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b396-v16-21","title":"供電區段與車載模式：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Supply-section and onboard states: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「供電區段與車載模式」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Supply-section and onboard states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"區分地面分段供電、架空線與車載儲能三種功能邊界，不把所有無架空線技術視為同一機制。用抽象狀態圖檢查模式資訊一致性，範例不重製廠商通電邏輯。布林狀態組合隨變數個數指數成長，這說明逐一人工檢查很快失去效率。可達性約束能排除不可能組合，但刪除條件必須有證據；安全性質通常針對所有可達狀態，而非幾個畫面上看起來合理的狀態。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「供電區段與車載模式」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish ground segments, overhead supply and onboard storage instead of treating all catenary-free systems as one mechanism. Check mode consistency in an abstract graph without reproducing supplier energization logic. Boolean combinations grow exponentially with variable count, explaining why manual enumeration soon becomes ineffective. Reachability constraints can eliminate impossible combinations, but each exclusion needs justification. Safety properties normally concern every reachable state rather than a few states that look plausible on a display. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Supply-section and onboard states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","failure":"常見誤解：「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「供電區段與車載模式」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Supply-section and onboard states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-21-k1","title":"供電區段與車載模式","titleEn":"Supply-section and onboard states","text":"區分地面分段供電、架空線與車載儲能三種功能邊界，不把所有無架空線技術視為同一機制。用抽象狀態圖檢查模式資訊一致性，範例不重製廠商通電邏輯。","textEn":"Distinguish ground segments, overhead supply and onboard storage instead of treating all catenary-free systems as one mechanism. Check mode consistency in an abstract graph without reproducing supplier energization logic.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「供電區段與車載模式」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Supply-section and onboard states\" is correct?","options":["區分地面分段供電、架空線與車載儲能三種功能邊界，不把所有無架空線技術視為同一機制。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Distinguish ground segments, overhead supply and onboard storage instead of treating all catenary-free systems as one mechanism.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"區分地面分段供電、架空線與車載儲能三種功能邊界，不把所有無架空線技術視為同一機制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish ground segments, overhead supply and onboard storage instead of treating all catenary-free systems as one mechanism. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b396-v16-22","title":"供電區段與車載模式：定量估算","titleEn":"Supply-section and onboard states: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「供電區段與車載模式」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Supply-section and onboard states” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。公式 y=2**bits，代入得 y=256 states。邊界：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Formula y=2**bits gives y=256 states. Boundary: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「供電區段與車載模式」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Supply-section and onboard states\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。","牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits.","Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：布林變數數量 bits=8 bits。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: number of Boolean state variables bits=8 bits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b396-v16-23","title":"供電區段與車載模式：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Supply-section and onboard states: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「供電區段與車載模式」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Supply-section and onboard states” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「供電區段與車載模式」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For supply-section and onboard states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「供電區段與車載模式」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for supply-section and onboard states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。以「供電區段與車載模式」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. For supply-section and onboard states, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把布林變數數量 bits 從 8 改成 9 bits（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 256 變為 512 states。先說明「供電區段與車載模式」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only number of Boolean state variables bits from 8 to 9 bits (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 256 to 512 states. Explain the causal direction for supply-section and onboard states, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「供電區段與車載模式」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Supply-section and onboard states\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍","用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.","Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用小型模型列舉轉移，再與需求允許的轉移表比較，對被排除狀態留下理由。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Enumerate transitions in a small model, compare against the required transition table, and document reasons for excluded states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b396-v16-24","title":"供電區段與車載模式：失效診斷","titleEn":"Supply-section and onboard states: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「供電區段與車載模式」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Supply-section and onboard states” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「供電區段與車載模式」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for supply-section and onboard states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：未限制的布林笛卡兒積；實際可達狀態通常較少，但需另證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Unconstrained Boolean Cartesian product; actual reachability can be smaller but must be established separately.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。回到「供電區段與車載模式」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Trace the input chain for supply-section and onboard states. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「供電區段與車載模式」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Supply-section and onboard states\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把感測器故障狀態預先刪掉會讓證明失去關鍵邊界，狀態抽象過粗也可能隱藏時序競爭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excluding sensor-fault states can remove the crucial boundary from a proof; overly coarse abstraction may hide timing races. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b396-v16-s4","title":"電源模式交接時序與備援電源共同原因","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing & Common causes in backup supplies","description":"本階段聚焦「電源模式交接時序」與「備援電源共同原因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Power-mode handoff timing\" and \"Common causes in backup supplies\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b396-v16-25","title":"電源模式交接時序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「電源模式交接時序」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Power-mode handoff timing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把來源辨識、介面處理和狀態確認分成可測事件，追蹤訊息何時真正被採用。總延遲只是教學預算，不能取代電氣保護與能量緩衝的獨立驗證。端到端延遲由量測、通訊、運算與致動串接而成。改善最快的一段通常影響有限，且平均延遲不能代表最壞尾端；定義一致的起訖事件，才能避免子系統都量到好看的數值卻漏掉交接等待。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電源模式交接時序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Split source identification, interface processing and confirmation into observable events and trace when information is used. The teaching timing budget does not replace independent protection or energy-buffer verification. End-to-end delay spans sensing, communication, computation and actuation. Improving the fastest stage often yields little benefit, and mean latency does not represent its worst tail. Consistent start and end events prevent subsystems from reporting attractive numbers while overlooking handoff queues. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Power-mode handoff timing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電源模式交接時序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Power-mode handoff timing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-25-k1","title":"電源模式交接時序","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing","text":"把來源辨識、介面處理和狀態確認分成可測事件，追蹤訊息何時真正被採用。總延遲只是教學預算，不能取代電氣保護與能量緩衝的獨立驗證。","textEn":"Split source identification, interface processing and confirmation into observable events and trace when information is used. The teaching timing budget does not replace independent protection or energy-buffer verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電源模式交接時序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Power-mode handoff timing\" is correct?","options":["每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短","把來源辨識、介面處理和狀態確認分成可測事件，追蹤訊息何時真正被採用。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.","Split source identification, interface processing and confirmation into observable events and trace when information is used.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把來源辨識、介面處理和狀態確認分成可測事件，追蹤訊息何時真正被採用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Split source identification, interface processing and confirmation into observable events and trace when information is used. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b396-v16-26","title":"電源模式交接時序：定量估算","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電源模式交接時序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Power-mode handoff timing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。公式 y=sense+network+compute+actuate，代入得 y=0.25 s。邊界：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Formula y=sense+network+compute+actuate gives y=0.25 s. Boundary: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電源模式交接時序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Power-mode handoff timing\", which statement holds?","options":["系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱","原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s。"],"optionsEn":["High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：量測時間 sense=0.03 s；網路時間 network=0.08 s；運算時間 compute=0.02 s；致動時間 actuate=0.12 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: sensing time sense=0.03 s; network time network=0.08 s; computation time compute=0.02 s; actuation time actuate=0.12 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b396-v16-27","title":"電源模式交接時序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電源模式交接時序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Power-mode handoff timing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「電源模式交接時序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For power-mode handoff timing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「電源模式交接時序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for power-mode handoff timing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。以「電源模式交接時序」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. For power-mode handoff timing, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把網路時間 network 從 0.08 改成 0.088 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.25 變為 0.258 s。先說明「電源模式交接時序」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only network time network from 0.08 to 0.088 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.25 to 0.258 s. Explain the causal direction for power-mode handoff timing, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電源模式交接時序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Power-mode handoff timing\"?","options":["沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同"],"optionsEn":["Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿同一事件編號串接時間戳，檢查每一段邊界是否重疊或漏算，並注入負載重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Follow one event identifier through timestamps, check stage boundaries for overlap or gaps, and repeat under injected load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b396-v16-28","title":"電源模式交接時序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Power-mode handoff timing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電源模式交接時序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Power-mode handoff timing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「電源模式交接時序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for power-mode handoff timing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：各階段串行且時間確定，沒有平行重疊或隨機尾端。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Deterministic serial stages without overlap or random latency tails.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。回到「電源模式交接時序」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Trace the input chain for power-mode handoff timing. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電源模式交接時序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Power-mode handoff timing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。","裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance.","Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間基準不同可造成負延遲假象；漏記排隊會使快速單元測試無法預測整合表現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different clock references can create apparently negative delays; omitted queues prevent fast unit tests from predicting integrated performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b396-v16-29","title":"備援電源共同原因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Common causes in backup supplies: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「備援電源共同原因」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Common causes in backup supplies” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"即使來源有兩種，轉換器、控制電源或冷卻路徑仍可能共用。先列共享介面再分析獨立失效，避免將設備數量增加誤認為風險自動歸零。兩支路都失效才失去功能的架構可降低獨立故障貢獻，卻不能消除共同原因。共同電源、相同軟體缺陷或同處淹水會同時影響兩支路；因此增加硬體數量不能取代分離、異質性與失效偵測的證據。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援電源共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two sources may still share converters, control power or cooling paths. Identify shared interfaces before analysing independent failures rather than assuming additional equipment eliminates risk. A function lost only when both branches fail can reduce independent contributions but cannot eliminate common causes. Shared power, identical software defects or flooding at one location can affect both branches. More hardware does not replace evidence for separation, diversity and fault detection. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Common causes in backup supplies” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「備援電源共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Common causes in backup supplies”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-29-k1","title":"備援電源共同原因","titleEn":"Common causes in backup supplies","text":"即使來源有兩種，轉換器、控制電源或冷卻路徑仍可能共用。先列共享介面再分析獨立失效，避免將設備數量增加誤認為風險自動歸零。","textEn":"Two sources may still share converters, control power or cooling paths. Identify shared interfaces before analysing independent failures rather than assuming additional equipment eliminates risk.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「備援電源共同原因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Common causes in backup supplies\" is correct?","options":["裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","即使來源有兩種，轉換器、控制電源或冷卻路徑仍可能共用。"],"optionsEn":["Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Two sources may still share converters, control power or cooling paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"即使來源有兩種，轉換器、控制電源或冷卻路徑仍可能共用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two sources may still share converters, control power or cooling paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b396-v16-30","title":"備援電源共同原因：定量估算","titleEn":"Common causes in backup supplies: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「備援電源共同原因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Common causes in backup supplies” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。公式 y=common+(1-common)*p*p，代入得 y=0.000104 1。邊界：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Formula y=common+(1-common)*p*p gives y=0.000104 1. Boundary: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「備援電源共同原因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Common causes in backup supplies\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。","牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快","直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1.","Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration.","Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：獨立支路失效機率 p=0.002 1；共同原因事件機率 common=0.0001 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: independent branch failure probability p=0.002 1; common-cause event probability common=0.0001 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b396-v16-31","title":"備援電源共同原因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Common causes in backup supplies: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「備援電源共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Common causes in backup supplies” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「備援電源共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in backup supplies, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「備援電源共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in backup supplies, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。以「備援電源共同原因」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. For common causes in backup supplies, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把共同原因事件機率 common 從 0.0001 改成 0.00011 1（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.000104 變為 0.000114 1。先說明「備援電源共同原因」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only common-cause event probability common from 0.0001 to 0.00011 1 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.000104 to 0.000114 1. Explain the causal direction for common causes in backup supplies, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「備援電源共同原因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Common causes in backup supplies\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。","外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces.","A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把獨立與共同原因兩類試驗分開，在隔離試驗台檢查共享介面失效的影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate independent and common-cause tests, using an isolated bench to examine failures of shared interfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b396-v16-32","title":"備援電源共同原因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Common causes in backup supplies: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「備援電源共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Common causes in backup supplies” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「備援電源共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in backup supplies. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：共同原因先發生的簡化條件模型，其餘支路相互獨立；非安全等級認證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Simple conditional model with common cause considered first and remaining branches independent; no safety-level certification is implied.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝設兩套相同設備就能完全消除共同原因故障」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing two identical systems completely removes common-cause failures.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。回到「備援電源共同原因」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Trace the input chain for common causes in backup supplies. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「備援電源共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Common causes in backup supplies\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共享電源中斷會讓看似雙備援同時失去功能，若故障偵測也共用同一支路更可能誤報正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of a shared supply can defeat apparently duplicated equipment, especially if fault detection depends on that same branch. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b396-v16-s5","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例與線路服務與設備修復","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases & Line service and equipment recovery","description":"本階段聚焦「潮濕污損與模式案例」與「線路服務與設備修復」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases\" and \"Line service and equipment recovery\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b396-v16-33","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「潮濕污損與模式案例」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把環境狀態與供電模式分成測試軸，不以乾燥正常運轉代表全部使用範圍。追溯每項需求的證據與未測邊界，數值算例不作為實際通電允許條件。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮濕污損與模式案例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Treat environmental condition and power mode as separate test axes rather than generalizing from dry normal operation. Trace requirement evidence and untested boundaries without using example values as energization permissions. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮濕污損與模式案例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-33-k1","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases","text":"把環境狀態與供電模式分成測試軸，不以乾燥正常運轉代表全部使用範圍。追溯每項需求的證據與未測邊界，數值算例不作為實際通電允許條件。","textEn":"Treat environmental condition and power mode as separate test axes rather than generalizing from dry normal operation. Trace requirement evidence and untested boundaries without using example values as energization permissions.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮濕污損與模式案例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases\" is correct?","options":["把環境狀態與供電模式分成測試軸，不以乾燥正常運轉代表全部使用範圍。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Treat environmental condition and power mode as separate test axes rather than generalizing from dry normal operation.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把環境狀態與供電模式分成測試軸，不以乾燥正常運轉代表全部使用範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Treat environmental condition and power mode as separate test axes rather than generalizing from dry normal operation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b396-v16-34","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例：定量估算","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮濕污損與模式案例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮濕污損與模式案例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases\", which statement holds?","options":["有回生制動的列車就不會產生任何制動熱","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","只要安培小時數相同任何兩種電池續航就一定相同"],"optionsEn":["A train with regenerative braking produces no braking heat.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","Equal ampere-hour ratings guarantee equal runtime for any two batteries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b396-v16-35","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮濕污損與模式案例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「潮濕污損與模式案例」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「潮濕污損與模式案例」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「潮濕污損與模式案例」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「潮濕污損與模式案例」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮濕污損與模式案例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","狀態變數多一個只會多出一種狀態組合","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding one Boolean state variable creates only one additional combination.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b396-v16-36","title":"潮濕污損與模式案例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮濕污損與模式案例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「潮濕污損與模式案例」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「潮濕污損與模式案例」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮濕污損與模式案例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wet, contaminated and mode-transition cases\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b396-v16-37","title":"線路服務與設備修復：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Line service and equipment recovery: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「線路服務與設備修復」如何影響無架空線輕軌供電的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Line service and equipment recovery” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Catenary-free light-rail power systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分開電源局部退出、車輛降級與全線停駛，才能解釋同樣故障對服務的不同影響。核對修復與恢復服務的時間點，避免可用度漂亮卻遮蔽功能受限。可用度描述長時間內能提供服務的比例，故障頻率與修復速度都會影響它。相同可用度可能來自頻繁短停或罕見長停，對旅客與維修資源的影響不同；更不能把高可用度直接解讀為故障發生時一定安全。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「線路服務與設備修復」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish local supply withdrawal, degraded vehicles and line suspension to explain different service consequences. Audit repair and service-restoration times so attractive availability cannot conceal reduced functionality. Availability describes the fraction of long-run time during which service is possible; both failure frequency and repair duration matter. The same value can arise from frequent brief outages or rare long ones with different passenger and maintenance consequences. High availability does not itself establish safe behaviour during failure. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Line service and equipment recovery” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「線路服務與設備修復」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Line service and equipment recovery”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-37-k1","title":"線路服務與設備修復","titleEn":"Line service and equipment recovery","text":"分開電源局部退出、車輛降級與全線停駛，才能解釋同樣故障對服務的不同影響。核對修復與恢復服務的時間點，避免可用度漂亮卻遮蔽功能受限。","textEn":"Distinguish local supply withdrawal, degraded vehicles and line suspension to explain different service consequences. Audit repair and service-restoration times so attractive availability cannot conceal reduced functionality.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線路服務與設備修復」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Line service and equipment recovery\" is correct?","options":["系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的","分開電源局部退出、車輛降級與全線停駛，才能解釋同樣故障對服務的不同影響。","牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快"],"optionsEn":["High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.","Distinguish local supply withdrawal, degraded vehicles and line suspension to explain different service consequences.","Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分開電源局部退出、車輛降級與全線停駛，才能解釋同樣故障對服務的不同影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish local supply withdrawal, degraded vehicles and line suspension to explain different service consequences. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b396-v16-38","title":"線路服務與設備修復：定量估算","titleEn":"Line service and equipment recovery: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「線路服務與設備修復」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Line service and equipment recovery” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。公式 y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)，代入得 y=0.998004 1。邊界：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Formula y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr) gives y=0.998004 1. Boundary: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。公式 y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr)，代入得 y=0.998004 1。邊界：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Formula y=mtbf/(mtbf+mttr) gives y=0.998004 1. Boundary: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「線路服務與設備修復」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Line service and equipment recovery\", which statement holds?","options":["直流電流增加兩倍時導線電阻損耗也只會增加兩倍","外殼溫度正常就能證明所有內部元件都沒有過熱","原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling DC current merely doubles resistive conductor loss.","A normal enclosure temperature proves that every internal component is free from overheating.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：平均故障間隔 mtbf=2000 h；平均修復時間 mttr=4 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean time between failures mtbf=2000 h; mean repair time mttr=4 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b396-v16-39","title":"線路服務與設備修復：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Line service and equipment recovery: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「線路服務與設備修復」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Line service and equipment recovery” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。以「線路服務與設備修復」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. For line service and equipment recovery, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把平均修復時間 mttr 從 4 改成 4.4 h（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.998004 變為 0.997805 1。先說明「線路服務與設備修復」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only mean repair time mttr from 4 to 4.4 h (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.998004 to 0.997805 1. Explain the causal direction for line service and equipment recovery, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。以「線路服務與設備修復」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. For line service and equipment recovery, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把平均修復時間 mttr 從 4 改成 4.4 h（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.998004 變為 0.997805 1。先說明「線路服務與設備修復」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only mean repair time mttr from 4 to 4.4 h (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.998004 to 0.997805 1. Explain the causal direction for line service and equipment recovery, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「線路服務與設備修復」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Line service and equipment recovery\"?","options":["分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","每個子系統平均很快就代表整體最壞延遲一定很短"],"optionsEn":["Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Fast average subsystems guarantee a short worst-case end-to-end delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別核對故障起點、服務恢復及完全修復時間，避免把部分恢復誤列為全功能。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit failure onset, service restoration and full repair separately rather than counting degraded service as full functionality. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b396-v16-40","title":"線路服務與設備修復：失效診斷","titleEn":"Line service and equipment recovery: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"prerequisiteIds":["b396-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「線路服務與設備修復」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Line service and equipment recovery” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。回到「線路服務與設備修復」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Trace the input chain for line service and equipment recovery. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：可修復二狀態穩態模型，未含共同原因故障、預防保養與供應鏈等待。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Repairable two-state steady model; common-cause failures, planned maintenance and supply-chain waiting are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「系統可用度很高就能直接證明所有故障都是安全的」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High system availability directly proves that every failure is safe.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b396-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。回到「線路服務與設備修復」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Trace the input chain for line service and equipment recovery. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]},{"id":"b396-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「線路服務與設備修復」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Line service and equipment recovery\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。","牽引電流變大就能保證車速增加得更快"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency.","Higher traction current guarantees a greater train acceleration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"刪除長停機紀錄會扭曲平均修復時間；重複報修同一缺陷則會錯估故障頻率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing long outages distorts mean repair time, while duplicate reports of one defect distort failure frequency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-aps-overview","v16s-aps-2018","v16s-aps-2021","v16s-rams-2002","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b396-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b396-en.svg"}};
